s, watercolors, perspective drawings, sketches, and photographs of construction projects to be submitted, “whose ultimate purpose is related to the training exercises of sport, such as stadiums, sports grounds, playgrounds, covered lanes, club buildings, boat houses, gymnasiums, bathhouses etc., and meet high artistic standards”. The exhibits for the two competitions, “" [:a {:href "/results/920030"} "Town Planning"] "” and “" [:a {:href "/results/920031"} "Architectural Designs"] "”, were identical, but were assessed separately for both categories. Therefore, works that were not awarded with a medal cannot be attributed to either category."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In architecture, all six medals were awarded. Probably for the first time, so-called “Honorable Mentions” were also expressed. The jury for architecture consisted of mostly well known architects from the USA."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Catalogue Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Translated Title"] [:th {} "Original Title"] [:th {} "Title in Olympic Report or Catalogue"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-primary"} [:abbrev {:title "Also Competed"} "AC"]]] [:td {:class "bib"} "15"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/920021"} "Hugo Gorge"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUT.png"}] "AUT"]] [:td {} "Competition for municipal bath in Wiener Neustadt (1st prize)"] [:td {} "Wettbewerb für das Stadtbad Wiener Neustadt (1. Preis)"] [:td {} "Wettbewerb für das Stadtbad Wiener-Neustadt (1. Preis)"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-primary"} [:abbrev {:title "Also Competed"} "AC"]]] [:td {:class "bib"} "16"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/920038"} "Alfred Keller"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AU